                          PicoSystem RDP Port
                  License and Redistribution Notice

This project ("PicoSystem RDP") is a personal, non-commercial port of the
Angrylion RDP renderer to the Pimoroni PicoSystem. The renderer core is
derived from Angrylion RDP Plus, which is itself derived from MESS / MAME
source code and is distributed under the MAME license.

Because the renderer core is a derivative work of MAME-licensed code, this
project as a whole inherits the MAME license terms for that derived core.
The MAME license is RESTRICTIVE with respect to redistribution and
commercial use. In particular:

  * Redistributions may not be sold, nor used in a commercial product or
    activity.
  * Redistributions modified from the original source must include the
    complete corresponding source code.
  * Redistributions must reproduce the MAME copyright notice, the list of
    conditions, and the disclaimer.

The full, verbatim MAME license text governing the Angrylion-derived
renderer core is reproduced in the NOTICE file in this repository.

This repository also bundles or depends on several third-party components
under their own (mostly permissive) licenses: ParaLLEl RDP (MIT), SDL
(zlib), Dear ImGui (MIT), the Raspberry Pi Pico SDK (BSD-3-Clause), the
PicoSystem SDK (MIT), the Adafruit ST7735/ST7789 library (MIT), and the
Orthodoxy clang-tidy plugin (GPL-3.0, build-time tooling only). The most
restrictive of these terms — the Angrylion-derived MAME-licensed core —
governs the project as a whole for redistribution purposes.

For the complete per-dependency breakdown (name, upstream, license type,
and how each component is used), see the NOTICE file. For prose discussion
of what derives from what and the redistribution constraint, see
docs/licensing.md. For attribution and credits, see CREDITS.md.

This is a personal port and is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or
licensed from MAME, Nicola Salmoria, or any upstream author.
